# SimpleOS fabricated `rt_*` baseline -- SHRINK-ONLY RATCHET (task #97)
#
# Format: one `<entry-key> <rt_symbol>` per line. `#` starts a comment.
# `<entry-key>` is the output binary's basename (see `simpleos_entry_key`).
#
# Semantics, enforced by `simpleos_check_no_fabricated_rt_stubs`:
#   the link FAILS when an entry's fabricated set is not a SUBSET of its
#   baseline. A missing file means an EMPTY baseline, i.e. maximum strictness --
#   deleting this file can never weaken the gate. An entry with no rows is
#   likewise maximally strict, so unmeasured entries are never fail-open.
#
# THIS IS NOT AN ALLOWLIST.
#   allowlist = `simpleos_rt_symbol_is_optional_backend`, a permanent semantic
#               claim that nil IS the correct answer for that symbol.
#   baseline  = this file: dated, per-entry, shrink-only debt that must go away.
# Never add a line here to make a new failure go away. New fabrication is the
# exact thing this gate exists to catch; implement the symbol, or justify it in
# the allowlist with a rationale naming the caller that treats nil as
# "unavailable". Every remediation wave DELETES lines here in the same commit
# that lands the implementation.
#
# CLASSIFY BY BODY, NEVER BY LINKAGE OR BY NAME.
#   Weak linkage does NOT imply fabricated: `baremetal_stubs.c` defines
#   rt_memcpy / rt_memset / rt_dma_alloc / rt_dma_phys_of / rt_dma_virt_of /
#   rt_file_read_bytes with `__attribute__((weak))` and REAL bodies. An earlier
#   revision built its "real" set with `extract_symbols_nm`, which drops W/w/V/v
#   outright, so all six were permanently unclassifiable as real and the guard
#   refused the link on the very entry its baseline was measured from. See
#   doc/08_tracking/bug/simpleos_fabricated_rt_guard_weak_real_false_positive_2026-07-28.md
#   Name prefixes are equally forbidden as a classifier: an `rt_simd_` prefix
#   allowlist would have swallowed `rt_engine2d_simd_*`, the real framebuffer
#   span blitters, which appear in the debt list below precisely because they
#   ARE fabricated on this arch.
#
# REGENERATION -- this procedure MUST stay identical to what the code does.
# (The previous mismatch between this comment and the implementation is exactly
# how the weak-real defect hid: the procedure used plain `nm`, which SHOWS weak
# definitions, while the code used `extract_symbols_nm`, which DROPS them.)
# Build the entry's boot objects with the same flags as
# `compile_simpleos_x86_64_c` (cc -c -m64 -ffreestanding -fno-pic -fno-pie
# -mno-red-zone -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections -O2), then:
#
#   REAL_OBJS = crt0.o baremetal_stubs.o type_stubs.o module_init.o
#               (auto_stubs.o is deliberately EXCLUDED -- being satisfied only
#                by that object is the condition being detected)
#
#   trivial  = `objdump -d --no-show-raw-insn REAL_OBJS` rt_* whose body is only
#              frame setup plus at most one constant materialisation
#              (`simpleos_trivial_body_rt_symbols`)
#   real     = `nm REAL_OBJS` defined symbols at ANY binding, i.e. skipping only
#              U/u and KEEPING W/w/V/v (`simpleos_defined_symbols_any_binding`),
#              MINUS `trivial`;  union  `nm <user objects>` defined symbols
#   refs     = `nm -u <user objects>` names beginning `rt_`
#              (`simpleos_undefined_rt_symbols`)
#
#   channel 1 = refs - real
#   channel 2 = trivial INTERSECT refs
#   fabricated = (channel 1 UNION channel 2) - simpleos_rt_symbol_is_optional_backend
#
# --- x86_64, measured 2026-07-28 against
# --- build/simpleos_wm_fullscreen_evidence/simpleos_wm_production_desktop.elf.
# --- Both channels measured, under the tightened allowlist in which
# --- `rt_arm_virtio_` is a SIX-NAME exact list rather than a prefix (the three
# --- sector-data-path symbols it used to swallow are now carried here as debt).
# --- Reproduced identically against all three retained user-object sets
# --- (native-objects-tJ7aAf/uSdrJr/wjwkwp, 689/679/680 objects): 55 fabricated
# --- under the old weak-dropping semantics, 49 under body classification, the
# --- same 6 weak-real symbols recovered each time.
# --- CAVEAT: the ELF's own object directory was not retained by the build, so
# --- these three 2026-07-22 object sets are the closest available proxy for the
# --- current link. They agree with each other exactly.
# --- Entries other than this one are not yet measured; they carry no rows and
# --- are therefore maximally strict, which is the intended ratchet behaviour.
simpleos_wm_production_desktop.elf rt_arm_virtio_blk_dma_base
simpleos_wm_production_desktop.elf rt_arm_virtio_blk_read_sector_direct
simpleos_wm_production_desktop.elf rt_arm_virtio_blk_sector_bytes
